.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt FS_USAGE 1
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm fs_usage
.Nd report file system activity as it happens
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl e
.Op Fl w
.Op Fl f Ar mode
.Op Fl t Ar seconds
.Op Ar pid | command ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows the file system (and network) system calls processes make, from the
kernel's trace, until it is interrupted or
.Fl t
seconds pass.
Each line has the time, the call, its file descriptor
.Pq Li F= ,
the bytes it moved
.Pq Li B= ,
or its error
.Pq Li [ Ns Ar errno Ns Li ] ,
the path the kernel looked up for it, how long it took in seconds, and the
process as
.Ar command Ns Li . Ns Ar pid .
Processes may be chosen by pid or command name;
.Fl e
excludes those instead.
.Nm
leaves itself out.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl w
Wide lines: microseconds and whole paths.
.It Fl f Ar mode
Only
.Cm filesys
calls,
.Cm network
calls,
.Cm exec
(execve and posix_spawn), or
.Cm pathname
(file system calls with a path); may be repeated.
.Cm diskio
and
.Cm cachehit
are taken as
.Cm filesys .
.It Fl t Ar seconds
Stop after that long.
.El
.Pp
It needs root, and the kernel's trace to itself while it runs.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtrace 1 ,
.Xr lsof 8
